snelling@bnr.ca (Peter Snelling) writes:

>I think some people find nethack far too difficult to even get started
>in.  Others know every little trick in the game, and now want more 
>complexity (eg NH++ (--)).  I think if we add several hundred new 
>monsters in each new version of nethack, the game will be far too
>tough for beginers.  I think what we may need is a user settable
>difficulty level.

Or do it the way Ularn does it: increase the level after each successful
completion. I.e. everyone starts at level 0, after the first completion of
the game, then all the next games start automatically at difficulty level 1.
The only thing that the difficulty level affects is regeneration. It is
possible to set the difficulty level at the command line.



